[h1]Phobos Framework[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.81.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

The shared toolbox behind the Phobos mods. On its own it adds no new machinery; install it with the Phobos content mods that need it, and it keeps their controls, crew work and supplies behaving the same way from one machine to the next.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Shared control panels explain what needs attention and what the crew can do. Apply or Discard settings, choose stores and standing orders, arrange training and set the volume for ready alerts.
[*]Crew standing orders: give crew a chosen job and approved supplies. Orders begin disabled; shifts, needs, access and the game's AutoTask and Haul duties still apply. Crew take supplies from anywhere aboard, nearest first, like the game's Reload job.
[*]Crew study Phobos specialities at powered terminals through the game's own study actions, and AutoTask crew choose them on their own.
[*]Supported onboard work carries on through time-skip. Exterior work and flight pause and wait for Resume.
[*]Construction, transfers and station purchases check materials, space and power. A full destination keeps cargo where it was.
[*]Shared gas and process-water lines (INSTALL, HVAC) and a conveyor belt (MISC). A line joins each machine or store it runs under or beside; touching equipment chains like pipe; nothing links over open floor. Lines hold what flows through them: drain one into a D20 canister (vent a gas line) before taking it up, and haul the canister to a tank to pour it in.
[*]Rivetline S2 to S5 process water silos for every mod, shared bulk storage in three sizes that shows its contents on right-click, canisters and suit bottles filled to 99%, honest mass, and station sales and 45% buy-back under the refuelling kiosk's Bulk supplies.
[*]RCS thrusters push by each gas's real cold-gas worth. Nitrogen flies exactly as before; oxygen and CO2 canisters give slightly less per kilogram, and RCS fuel readings count in nitrogen-equivalent kilograms. Content mods can add their own propellant feeds.
[*]When a Phobos autopilot switches ship sensors on, it remembers what it switched and turns off only those. Your own switch always wins, and you are told every time in the crew log and on the nav map.
[*]Content mods can lay the game's own build sites for destroyed parts, vanilla or modded; the crew still build them with real parts.
[*]Shared merchant stock, faction-kiosk scrip offers gated by reputation, salvage finds, mining-find shares, repair, Restore and dismantling rules for the content mods.
[*]Shared translations.
[*]Data packs: a content mod's tables (prices, work, salvage, offers, recipes, materials, store ratings, machine sizes) ship as readable files and accept your own override files in BepInEx/config, merged by name and checked before use; machine sizes and connection points are read-only. Every recipe must conserve mass, and a shipped recipe revision never changes: a new one is added beside it. See the editing guide.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Install Framework together with Phobos Shipbreaker, Auto Nav, Agriculture, Manufacturing or War Has Been Declared. Each content mod names the Framework version it needs.
[*]Right-click Phobos equipment and choose Control Panel for its settings and crew orders.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosframework status reports what loaded; phobosframework crew shows who is studying or could take each order step, and why; phobosframework loot shows a mining table as the game rolls it now.
[/list]
Mod authors: see the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/development/framework-author-guide.md]Framework author guide[/url].

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Optional: Valtora's Ship's Water (its tanks join and fill water lines), LOGUSS's Common Sense modules and jossla's Study at Terminals work alongside it.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Framework and the Phobos content mods you want.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[*]Used the repository's local installer before? Remove those local copies first so only one copy loads. See the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/installing-mods.md]installation guide[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
Ordinary saves are supported. Keep Framework and the content mods installed while a save uses their content; removing them is not a clean uninstall. Updating does not refill existing shops or old loot containers. Saved contents or settings that cannot be checked safely stop the affected work for inspection. A pipe that just broke is noticed within two seconds. A player data file that breaks a rule is skipped with the reason in the log and on the F3 console; the shipped values stand. Automated checks pass; in-game evaluation of recent features is ongoing.

